        "created_at": 1794501306.6680543
      },
      "rev_n_2_3c6cf5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_3c6cf5_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_3c6cf5",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy algorithm to always pick the two cheapest items that do not exceed X when added together.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501306.668068
      },
      "rev_n_3_82a02a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_82a02a_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_82a02a",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total number of pairs of items whose combined price is greater than X and subtract this from the total number of items.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501306.668076
      },
      "rev_n_2_3c6cf5_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_3c6cf5_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_3c6cf5",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1 (revised): Instead of trying to ensure no pairs sum up to more than X, focus on marking as many items as possible without creating any valid pairs that could lead to a free unicorn horn. This means selecting items such that no two items in the selected set have a combined price greater than X. One effective strategy is to select items in descending order based on their prices, ensuring that the highest-priced item does not form a valid pair with any other item in the set.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_3c6cf5_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_4545c28f24",
        "created_at": 1794501318.5349712
      },
      "rev_n_3_82a02a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_82a02a_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_82a02a",
        "thought_text": "The issue arises because the current approach counts pairs where the sum of the prices is greater than \\(X\\) but does not ensure that no pair can ever sum up to exactly \\(X\\). To fix this, we need to exclude items that could potentially form a valid pair with any other item to sum up to \\(X\\).\n\nA better strategy is to identify items that, when paired with any other item, would result in a sum equal to \\(X\\). We can do this by iterating through the sorted list and checking if there exists another item that, when added to the current item, equals \\(X\\). If such an item exists, we should exclude both from consideration since they cannot be part of a valid pair.\n\nHere's the corrected thought process:\n\n1. Sort the list of item prices.\n2. Iterate through the sorted list and for each item, check if there exists another item in the list such that their sum equals \\(X\\).\n3. If such an item exists, exclude both from consideration.\n4. Count the remaining items, which are the ones that can be part of the special offer without forming a valid pair that sums up to \\(X\\).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_82a02a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b864ecebc0",
        "created_at": 1794501339.5186226
      },
      "rev_n_4_b83ab7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_b83ab7_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_b83ab7",
        "thought_text": "Select the largest items and exclude them from the offer.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8234543949888363",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501348.526881
      },
      "rev_n_5_d82b5b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_d82b5b_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_d82b5b",
        "thought_text": "Pair the cheapest items together and exclude any other pairs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8234543949888363",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501348.526899
      },
      "rev_n_6_268c7c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_268c7c_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_268c7c",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy algorithm to select items based on their individual value relative to X.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8234543949888363",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501348.5269108
      },
      "rev_n_5_d82b5b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_d82b5b_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_d82b5b",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of pairing the cheapest items together, consider marking items individually as long as they do not exceed the minimum cost \\(X\\) when paired with any other item. This ensures no pair can meet the criteria for receiving a free unicorn horn.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8234543949888363",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_d82b5b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0da06b6901",
        "created_at": 1794501359.7371967
      },
      "rev_n_7_2ca34b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_2ca34b_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_2ca34b",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through the sorted list and keep adding items to the offer set until adding another item would violate the condition.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "636808690586209895",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501381.180135
